r","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, September to October has come in under 90% of normal in 36 of the 75 years since 1951 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids ran 66% of normal in August to September and 169% in May to June. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 63% and March to April at 141% on the middle of the grids. Grid 26019 had its driest year in 1980 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
